        "original_id": "62ce9bbc-560e-5899-9fbb-2877afcddfb1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: TRS-80 Color Computer, Interact Home Computer\n- Companies: Radio Shack, Tandy, Interact Electronics Inc\n- Places: Ann Arbor, Michigan\n- Concepts: home computers, Motorola 6809 processor\n\nFacts:\n- In 1978, the Interact Home Computer was introduced as a very early American home computer.\n- Interact Electronics Inc made the Interact Home Computer in Ann Arbor, Michigan.\n- The TRS-80 Color Computer is a line of home computers.\n- Radio Shack marketed the TRS-80 Color Computer, and Tandy also marketed it as the Tandy Color Computer.\n- The TRS-80 Color Computer was affectionately nicknamed CoCo.\n- The TRS-80 Color Computer line was based on the Motorola 6809 processor.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
